  "review_fixes": [
    "Natural native Git exit is observed without reaping, then owned streams drain before reap; no numeric process-group signal is sent after normal reap.",
    "Cleanup uncertainty is reported promptly while the owned supervisor retains repository and admission holders.",
    "The russh channel remains retained until native exit status, EOF and close are delivered or delivery fails; dropping the pumps cannot close it first.",
    "HTTP shutdown now stops admission and owns connection draining, with a deadline and joined cancellation instead of leaving idle keep-alive tasks detached.",
    "The host-key fixture shares the existing sanitized Git command helper.",
    "Existing denied-read operating cases additionally require empty ref output, with a subsequent allowed control and unchanged repository state.",
    "The setup guide distinguishes the server host key from a passphrase-protected client key, registers only the public key and names the clone destination."
  ],
